maria: opened a docs PR to consolidate and modernize SDK snippets for streaming, retries, and pagination across py/ts/go. PR link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/4599. main goals: standardize retry policy examples, show async streaming in python, cursor resume patterns for embeddings, and add go context + iterator pattern.

alex: thanks — does this change any public SDK interfaces or just examples?

maria: only examples. small rename alignment: 'max_retries' -> 'retries' in snippets to match the SDK arg. noted in the PR description.

